{
  "schema": "lr.amusements/1",
  "_note": "Arcade machines and carnival booths the runner can play (game/instruments/amusements.rs; a Rust addition, Godot's booths are separate minigames). kinds: prop type -> prompt (shown after the interact key), press (the cue played at once; any carnival_* or music_* cue of the cue table), result_seconds (how long after the press the result comes), win and lose (each optional: cue, text for the message line; win also has chance 0..1 and coins, a small prize paid at most once per machine and at most prize.max_per_run times a run), noise and noise_seconds (the runner's noise burst the hunters hear, in the units of walking 4.2 and sprinting 10.5) and an optional cooldown_seconds of its own. cooldown_seconds: one play per machine per this long. noise_enabled false leaves only the sound. reach: metres from the prop's centre (the booths are up to 2.5 m wide); aim_height: the height the crosshair is matched against. Nothing here is sent to other players: the sound, the message and the prize are the pressing runner's own.",
  "cooldown_seconds": 1.5,
  "noise_enabled": true,
  "reach": 2.2,
  "aim_height": 1.2,
  "prize": { "max_per_run": 5 },
